Hi Vilis,

I'm glad to see that you have found the user group.

If the fitted model is accurate down to 20 minute resolution and over several years, then there is absolutely no problem with gaps other than that they imply less data. All of the intermediate times are marginalized from the complete likelihood function without any approximations. This is one of the benefits of continuous-time analysis.

Best,
Chris

